Comment:
 MP3 encoding is provided by LAME 3.100, reached through the mp3lame-encoder
 and mp3lame-sys crates. mp3lame-sys does NOT link a system libmp3lame.so: it
 vendors LAME's C source and compiles it in, so every Baxters Stereo Mix binary
 CONTAINS LAME. Verified on the shipped binary rather than assumed — it imports
 zero LAME symbols from any shared library and defines them internally.
 .
 Static linkage is the case the LGPL is most concerned with, because a user
 cannot simply drop in their own build of the library. LGPL-3 section 4(d)
 therefore requires either a shared-library mechanism, or that the user be given
 what they need to relink the application against a modified LAME.
 .
 THIS PACKAGE SATISFIES THAT BY SHIPPING ITS COMPLETE SOURCE, at
 /opt/baxters/stereo-mix/source/baxters-stereo-mix-source.tar.gz, under the MIT
 licence above. Anyone can substitute a modified LAME and rebuild.
 .
 That is not decoration. The project's own THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES states that the
 compliance argument holds only while the source travels with the work, and
 names this exact situation: "If Stereo Mix is ever shipped as a binary WITHOUT
 its source, this stops being true." A .deb is precisely that event, so the
 source is included in the package rather than merely offered elsewhere.
 .
 LAME is used exactly as vendored; nothing here patches it. Full notices travel
 in /opt/baxters/stereo-mix/licenses/ and THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.
 .
 Baxters Stereo Mix uses the LAME MP3 encoder — https://lame.sourceforge.io/ .
 LAME's own LICENSE asks that projects using it say so; freely given.

